---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Control Responsibility Matrix | BeaconGuard Assurance"
  description="BeaconGuard responsibility boundaries across AI Provider, Enterprise Application, BeaconGuard authorization, Enterprise System of Record, and Customer Governance."
>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <h1>Control Responsibility Matrix</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This page helps reviewers understand which responsibilities BeaconGuard
      owns, which remain with the enterprise application and system of record,
      and which stay with customer governance. It is intended to reduce
      ambiguity during architecture, security, risk, and procurement review.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Responsibility model</h2>
    <p>
      BeaconGuard authorizes whether an enterprise application may invoke an AI
      provider and whether a declared enterprise action based on an AI-generated
      result may proceed under the Active Verified Release. Runtime outcomes are
      ALLOW or DENY only. BeaconGuard does not replace transaction systems,
      systems of record, or model providers. Review does not mutate a DENY into
      ALLOW.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>AI Provider:</strong> Produces the model result.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Enterprise Application:</strong> Declares the intended action
        and provides required context; executes only an authorized action.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>BeaconGuard:</strong> Authorizes or denies the proposed use
        under the Active Verified Release; records evidence; provides Verify.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Enterprise System of Record:</strong> Remains authoritative for
        resulting business state.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Customer Governance:</strong> Retains clinical, legal,
        operational, compliance, and business judgment.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Responsibility Matrix</h2>
    <div class="responsibility-matrix-wrap">
      <table class="responsibility-matrix">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Responsibility</th>
            <th>AI Provider</th>
            <th>Enterprise Application</th>
            <th>BeaconGuard</th>
            <th>Enterprise System of Record</th>
            <th>Customer Governance</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Model result production</td>
            <td>Owns serving and produces the AI-generated result</td>
            <td>Invokes the provider only after Request Admission ALLOW</td>
            <td>Does not produce model output</td>
            <td>Does not produce model output</td>
            <td>Evaluates suitability of provider use</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Request Admission Authorization</td>
            <td>Does not own admission policy</td>
            <td>Submits trusted request context and enforces returned decision</td>
            <td>Owns ALLOW or DENY for provider invocation under Active Verified Release</td>
            <td>Does not own request authorization</td>
            <td>Reviews boundary correctness and playbook fit</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Declare intended enterprise action</td>
            <td>Does not declare enterprise actions</td>
            <td>Declares the intended action and provides required context</td>
            <td>Does not invent or guess the intended action</td>
            <td>Does not declare the action</td>
            <td>Defines acceptable action contracts</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Result-to-Action Authorization</td>
            <td>Does not authorize enterprise effect</td>
            <td>Requests authorization for the declared action; respects DENY</td>
            <td>Owns ALLOW or DENY for the declared intended action</td>
            <td>Does not authorize the action</td>
            <td>Reviews action-control fit and residual risk</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Execute authorized action</td>
            <td>Does not execute enterprise actions</td>
            <td>Executes only an authorized action</td>
            <td>Does not execute business transactions</td>
            <td>May receive resulting business updates</td>
            <td>Validates control separation and escalation paths</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Business state authority</td>
            <td>Out of scope</td>
            <td>Orchestrates workflow against systems of record</td>
            <td>Does not become the system of record</td>
            <td>Remains authoritative for resulting business state</td>
            <td>Owns clinical, legal, operational, and business judgment</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Decision evidence and Verify</td>
            <td>Does not provide BeaconGuard decision evidence</td>
            <td>Correlates decisions with workflow context as needed</td>
            <td>Emits Verifiable Decision Records; Verify remains read-only</td>
            <td>May hold downstream business records, not BeaconGuard evidence by default</td>
            <td>Reviews evidence; must not treat AI insights as authority</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Fail-closed and non-AI fallback</td>
            <td>Does not control BeaconGuard fail-closed semantics</td>
            <td>Must enforce DENY; owns non-AI fallback behavior</td>
            <td>Returns DENY when required conditions are missing or out of bounds</td>
            <td>Not responsible for request or action gating</td>
            <td>Validates that failure handling is explicit and reviewable</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What reviewers should verify</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The application submits the trusted request context BeaconGuard requires
      </li>
      <li>
        Request Admission ALLOW or DENY is enforced before provider invocation
      </li>
      <li>
        The intended enterprise action is declared by the application, not
        inferred from model content as authority
      </li>
      <li>
        Result-to-Action ALLOW or DENY is enforced before enterprise effect
      </li>
      <li>
        Review does not mutate a DENY into ALLOW; later authorization uses a new
        governed request where applicable
      </li>
      <li>Provider success is not treated as enterprise authorization</li>
      <li>Systems of record remain authoritative for business state</li>
      <li>
        Verify is read-only and AI-assisted insights are non-authoritative
      </li>
      <li>
        Customer governance retains clinical, legal, operational, compliance,
        and business judgment
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Next step</h2>
    <p>
      Reviewers can continue structured evaluation through the Reviewer Kit,
      Trust Center, and Contact path.
    </p>
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/reviewer-kit">Open Reviewer Kit</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/trust-assurance">Review Trust Center</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/contact">Continue via contact</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
